{"author":{"id":"6d85cf2fcebaeefd8c5c528f2d5f5f98f26ce3275422d0dc5f7c0fd596f9f59f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791591146,"nonce":"IuCp+gjRCAaAIUaGUHJ/5SL3vbg=","title":"Borders take layout space on the HashLink path","message":"A border width inset only the paint on the HashLink path; owned contexts already wrote Taffy's border in set_border. The user decided borders take layout space, as in CSS.\n\n**Change**\nWhen a flush applies a BorderWidth render write, the node's Taffy border is set from the widths as painted (each side's own width, or the shared one), and layout is marked dirty. The paint props stay the one source, so unsetting a side falls back to the shared width without a separate record.\n\n**Effect, from ashui snapshots**\n- A child that fills a bordered box sits inside the border instead of painting over it.\n- Boxes sized by content grow by twice the border; fixed-size boxes keep their size.\n- With overflow hidden, nothing changes: the clip already stopped at the border's inner edge.\n- ashui's checkbox marks moved off-centre (see below); the rest is the CSS sizing above.\n\n**Taffy: auto margins on an absolute child with a border**\nAn absolute child with inset 0 and margin auto, in an 18px box with a 2px border, is placed at 6,6; CSS places it at 4,4. Taffy measures the insets from the padding box but resolves the auto margins over the border box. Flex alignment (no insets) centres correctly. ashui's checkbox marks now centre by alignment. The bug is upstream in Taffy.","files":null}]}